WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:05.279
How long do we have to wait to see Mark Wahlberg
sporting Sully's iconic mustache?

00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:07.570
And what's up with that prison scene?

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:09.440
Here's what happens at the end of "Uncharted."

00:00:10.799 --> 00:00:14.940
Based on the beloved video game franchise,
"Uncharted" serves as an origin story for

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:18.539
rugged adventurer Nathan Drake, played by
Tom Holland.

00:00:18.539 --> 00:00:23.039
Nathan is a street-smart bartender in New
York when he's approached by Mark Wahlberg's

00:00:23.039 --> 00:00:28.490
Victor "Sully" Sullivan about teaming up to
find the lost gold of Ferdinand Magellan.

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:33.450
Sully explains that he was originally partnered
with Nate's brother Sam, who appeared in "Uncharted

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:35.790
4" and "Uncharted: The Lost Legacy."

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.090
"I think you're here because of your brother."

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:39.680
"Wait, you know my brother Sam?"

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:43.720
While Nate hasn't heard from Sam in years,
he can't help but be intrigued by the prospect

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:48.360
of finding the treasure Sam told him about
when he was a child and possibly discovering

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.770
what happened to his long-lost sibling.

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:55.511
Competing with Sully and Nate to find the
gold is the ruthless Santiago Moncada and

00:00:55.511 --> 00:00:57.860
a deadly mercenary named Braddock.

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:02.450
However, by the time the entire cast of characters
is on a plane bound for the Philippines at

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:07.109
the end of the second act, Braddock shows
her true colors, slitting Moncada's throat

00:01:07.109 --> 00:01:08.929
so she can collect the treasure herself.

00:01:08.929 --> 00:01:13.900
It's at this point that she and her henchmen
catch on to the presence of Nate, Sully, and

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:16.619
their ally Chloe, who have stowed away.

00:01:16.619 --> 00:01:20.560
Their fight in the cargo bay leads to the
film's most eye-popping set piece in which

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:24.070
Nate is swept out of the plane with several
large crates.

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:28.940
When he finally manages to make it back, things
go from bad to worse, leading to the film's

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.210
final act.

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:34.960
Nate climbs the boxes of cargo and dives back
into the plane.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:39.969
However, before he can settle down for even
a second, Chloe, who is also battling Braddock

00:01:39.969 --> 00:01:44.810
and her goons in the cargo hold, drives into
him and out of the plane in Moncada's little

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:47.579
red sports car in an effort to escape.

00:01:47.579 --> 00:01:51.210
Things don't look good for either of them
for a moment, but Chloe soon reveals that

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.630
she has a parachute.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:56.210
Through a stroke of good luck, she manages
to save herself and Nate.

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:59.759
They make it safely to the ground — but
they're in the middle of the ocean sitting

00:01:59.759 --> 00:02:01.399
on top of a box of cargo.

00:02:01.399 --> 00:02:05.420
Fortunately, they spot a crowded beach, and
then find a room for the night.

00:02:06.619 --> 00:02:10.330
Throughout the movie, Nate reads and re-reads
the postcards his brother Sam sent to him

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:11.560
through the years.

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:16.390
These are postcards Nate now knows Sam sent
while he was working with Sully to find Magellan's

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:17.390
gold.

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:21.310
Now that Sully has told him his brother is
dead, they're more precious to him than ever.

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:25.200
As Nate looks over the map and the two crosses
that serve as keys to the location of the

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.720
treasure, he turns his attention back to Sam's
postcards.

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:32.920
He then thinks of something that hadn't occurred
to him before: Sam could have left him a clue

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:35.280
to finding the gold in one of the postcards.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:39.420
In the flashback scene that starts the movie
reminiscent of the flashback from Uncharted

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:44.080
4, Sam leaves Nate a secret message when he
escapes from the orphanage where they live.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:47.940
Young Nate uncovers the message by shining
the flame from a lighter on the back of the

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:50.160
paper where the message was embedded.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:55.390
Now, Nate uses the same technique on Sam's
postcards and discovers his brother did, indeed,

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:57.080
leave him a hidden message.

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:01.510
The invisible ink he finds on one of the postcards
tells him that the crosses can also serve

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:02.510
as a compass.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:08.220
Just as Sam seemingly intended, Nate uses
the crosses to find the coordinates of the

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:09.220
treasure.

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:12.860
Now that he knows exactly where to go to get
the gold, he has to decide whether to share

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:14.360
the news with Chloe.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:18.700
Throughout the movie, Nate has been quick
to trust, especially when it comes to Chloe,

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:20.190
and he's paid the price repeatedly.

00:03:20.190 --> 00:03:25.010
Now, however, it seems that Nate finally realizes
that he can't trust Chloe to stay loyal to

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:27.730
him or keep his best interests at heart.

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:32.040
So before he goes to sleep, he leaves out
a set of fake coordinates for Chloe to find

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:33.970
in case she wakes up before him.

00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:37.160
Just as Nate suspected she might, Chloe takes
the bait.

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:41.470
When Nate wakes up, Chloe is nowhere to be
found and the fake coordinates are gone.

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:46.140
While Chloe is off on a wild goose chase,
Nate takes a boat and speeds out to the location

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:49.500
of the actual coordinates, a cave in the middle
of the ocean.

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:54.100
However, when Nate gets there, he discovers
that the cave doesn't contain just one ship,

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.100
but two.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:59.620
Nate boards one of Magellan's timeworn ships
and starts to explore.

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:03.650
As he does, Sully arrives and is delighted
to find that the ship contains barrels full

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:04.650
of gold.

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:09.370
Between that and the value of the historical
ships, Sully knows he's in for quite a payday.

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:10.370
After all,

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:13.030
"It's the biggest treasure that's never been
found."

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:17.340
Unfortunately, the celebration is short-lived
because Braddock and her henchmen appear in

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:18.479
the cave.

00:04:18.479 --> 00:04:22.830
Nate and Sully are vastly outnumbered, so
they hide in the ship as Braddock takes in

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:24.009
her discovery.

00:04:24.009 --> 00:04:28.449
As they wait, presumably, for her to take
what she wants and go, Nate and Sully realize

00:04:28.449 --> 00:04:31.300
Braddock has something else in mind entirely.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:35.520
She has summoned two large helicopters to
fly the intact boats out of the cave so she

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:38.199
can bring every bit of the treasure back with
her.

00:04:38.199 --> 00:04:42.169
After each helicopter is attached to one of
the ships with ropes, they begin to lift the

00:04:42.169 --> 00:04:45.900
ships out of the open ceiling of the cave
and start toward their destination.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:51.889
Since the ships are now completely in Braddock's
control, Nate and Sully are going to be revealed

00:04:51.889 --> 00:04:54.770
eventually, so the two know they're going
to have to fight.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:58.389
Since Braddock and her henchman are on the
ships as they're being transported, it's not

00:04:58.389 --> 00:05:00.580
long until a full-on brawl starts.

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:04.740
While Braddock and her henchmen don't hesitate
to attack Nate and Sully once they reveal

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:09.479
themselves, the duo is every bit as determined
as Braddock to get the treasure.

00:05:09.479 --> 00:05:13.020
Even though the pair know the other ship is
lost to them, they do everything they can

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:15.650
to establish control of the ship they're on.

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:21.020
This results in a battle involving clubs,
guns, swords, knives, fists, and anything

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:22.810
else the combatants can use.

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:27.330
In the end, Braddock's henchmen are vanquished
and Sully manages to gain control of the helicopter

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:28.860
carrying the ship.

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:33.060
However, Braddock is still standing and Nate
turns to face her as the ropes holding the

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:34.919
ship to the helicopter start to give out.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:39.810
Nate and Braddock know they don't want to
be on the ship when the ropes break, so they

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:43.410
start to climb the ship's masts and the ropes
attached to the helicopter.

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:47.249
Ultimately, whether or not either of them
makes it out of the situation comes down to

00:05:47.249 --> 00:05:48.539
Sully in the helicopter.

00:05:48.539 --> 00:05:52.969
Yet, Sully also has his hands on a bag full
of gold, which may be more important to him

00:05:52.969 --> 00:05:55.860
than anything, including Nate's life.

00:05:55.860 --> 00:06:01.530
Nate scrambles toward the helicopter and reaches
out his hand to Sully, but Sully pauses.

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:05.360
Just when it looks like he's going to let
Nate fall with the ship, Sully drops the gold

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:08.160
and grabs Nate's hand, pulling him to safety.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:11.300
The bag of gold falls into the ocean, along
with Braddock.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:15.819
Then, the ropes attaching the ship to the
helicopter finally break and the boat crashes

00:06:15.819 --> 00:06:18.520
into the sea, right on top of Braddock.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:20.930
For a glorious moment, the ship floats on
the water.

00:06:20.930 --> 00:06:25.529
Then, as Nate and Sully watch from above,
the ship crumbles and slowly sinks into the

00:06:25.529 --> 00:06:26.529
ocean.

00:06:26.529 --> 00:06:30.449
Nate suggests they could still salvage the
treasure from beneath the sea, but Sully points

00:06:30.449 --> 00:06:33.840
out a Filipino government boat is already
on the scene.

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:37.220
There's no way he and Nate could get to the
treasure before they do.

00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:40.849
Just when it looks like they're going to go
home empty-handed, Nate reveals he's stashed

00:06:40.849 --> 00:06:44.440
several pieces of gold in his pockets as a
thrilled Sully flies them away.

00:06:46.389 --> 00:06:50.529
While Nate and Sully's first cinematic adventure
together has ended, Nate still doesn't know

00:06:50.529 --> 00:06:52.800
all the details about what happened to his
brother.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:57.441
At one point in the movie, Braddock indicates
that she killed him, and Chloe and Sully make

00:06:57.441 --> 00:06:59.879
it clear that they both believe Sam is dead.

00:06:59.879 --> 00:07:03.520
However, the final few moments of the film
reveal that none of the characters really

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:05.930
know the truth about Sam's fate.

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:07.970
The scene cuts to a dark prison.

00:07:07.970 --> 00:07:12.990
In a small cell shrouded in shadows, a prisoner
with long, unkempt blonde hair is writing

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:17.050
a postcard that looks like those Nate had
previously received from his brother.

00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:20.930
Although the camera never gives us a good
look at his face, this must be Sam.

00:07:20.930 --> 00:07:25.379
Beyond that, the postcard he's writing seems
to indicate he's been trying to contact Nate

00:07:25.379 --> 00:07:29.780
for a while, but he's not sure his messages
have actually been getting through.

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:31.949
Following that brief glimpse, the credits
roll.

00:07:33.150 --> 00:07:37.789
Finally, in a mid-credits scene, the movie
sets up a potential "Uncharted" sequel.

00:07:37.789 --> 00:07:41.479
Nate is seen meeting with a man with an eyepatch
in what looks like a tropical cafe.

00:07:41.479 --> 00:07:46.180
They are there to make an exchange: the ring
Nate wears on a strap around his neck in exchange

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:49.589
for a Nazi map that presumably leads to a
new treasure.

00:07:49.589 --> 00:07:53.509
Just as it seems like the negotiations are
about to go south and Nate is preparing to

00:07:53.509 --> 00:07:58.180
fight the man's allies, who have him surrounded,
Sully shows up with a gun and the pair regain

00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:00.479
control of the situation.

00:08:00.479 --> 00:08:05.330
Nate grabs the map and throws Sully, who's
now sporting a mustache and a cigar.

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:09.629
Sully sniffs the cigar appreciatively as Nate
joins him at the door only to show the man

00:08:09.629 --> 00:08:12.870
with the eyepatch that he's also taken back
his ring.

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:17.219
As the pair walk out together, Nate expresses
his annoyance with Sully, who was supposed

00:08:17.219 --> 00:08:18.830
to arrive the day before.

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:23.469
However, Sully explains he was late because
he had a hard time getting his cat, Mr. Whiskers,

00:08:23.469 --> 00:08:26.789
who he's now carrying in a backpack, through
customs.

00:08:26.789 --> 00:08:29.620
As they talk, the pair turn and stop dead
in their tracks.

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:33.959
Whatever they see in front of them seems to
startle them both, but before we can see what

00:08:33.959 --> 00:08:38.690
it is, the sequence cuts, and the rest of
the credits unspool.

